  "evidenceNotes": {
    "table32And56": "Each section is a count, that many eight-byte (relative offset, count) slots, then that many values: AssetInfo uses 24 bytes and Bundle uses 48. Selected native readers use unsigned comparer-hash modulo capacity, the slot range and these value strides; current stored keys themselves map by unsigned key modulo capacity. Current file slots tile all values once; dictionary Bundle values join array Bundles by name and semantic fields except bundleIndex is zero in the dictionary. Asset path offsets reference Brotli UTF-16 strings that tile the terminal variable suffix, but path strings can repeat and no AssetMap/GUID ownership join follows from names alone. Source writer, native lookups and full current-file replay substantiate this layout; live gameplay lookup execution remains unresolved.",
    "hashVersion": "Writer starts from hashName and folds rawData.deps name hashes with multiply 39 and XOR. The authenticated managed UTF-16 fallback reproduces every current row through the actual Burst call route; unseen strings and Burst case behavior remain conditional. Runtime comparisons remain unresolved.",
    "execution": "Static selected-build initializer and accessor path. Both BundleLoader+Manager sync and async proxy loaders call the named direct-dependency accessor, then have a loop-element read and self-recursion; no live ref/out capture, branch execution or authored-edge cause established."
  }
